    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0594" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg566"/>

                <head>299. Telegram From the Embassy in Egypt to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d299-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-04-21T11:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                                1956—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2104. For the Secretary. In re-reading Embassy telegram 2087,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d299-f2"/> am concerned that point (6) of last paragraph might be
                    misunderstood. What I had in mind was what positive acts we would wish Nasser to make, as contrasted to those
                    things he is doing which he should not do. Some of latter at least are easy to
                    define and we will, <pb facs="0595" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/> of course, keep
                    working away at these without necessity specific instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Byroade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
